              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "tarati comes from the root √tṝ \"cross over\", and then \"float, swim\" (CDIAL 5702). The root is inherited from Indo-European (EtymDB), and MW sets it beside Latin trans \"across\" and terminus \"boundary\". It lives on as Hindi tarnā \"to cross\" and Punjabi tarnā \"to swim\" (CDIAL 5702)."
